  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(5a + (4)/(a) - 2) = 13\n\n**Concept used:**\n\n(a + b)² = a² + b² + 2ab \n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ (5a + (4)/(a)) = 13 + 2\n\n⇒ (5a + (4)/(a)) = 15\n\nSquaring both sides\n\n⇒ (5a + (4)/(a))² = 15²\n\n⇒ 25a² + (16/a²) + 2 × 5a × (4/a) = 225\n\n⇒ 25a2 + (16/a2) + 40 = 225\n\n⇒ 25a2 + (16/a2) = 225 - 40\n\n⇒ (25a2 + (16)/(a²)) = 185\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 185.**",
